  "_design_notes": {
    "purpose": "Ten stakeholders shaped so Appendix A's four scenarios produce the exact matrix rows they are meant to. The arithmetic below is load-bearing; changing a tier or an on_call flag changes which decision row fires.",
    "scoring": "qualification = DOMAIN_POINTS[fit] + 8 * seniority_tier + (15 if on_call) where DOMAIN_POINTS = {primary: 100, secondary: 55}",
    "infrastructure_matches": "7 of 10 — 3 primary (Priya, Tom, Elena) + 4 secondary (Marcus, Aisha, Daniel, Yuki)",
    "critical_floor": "max(120, incumbent - 25). With Priya at 139 the floor is 120: only Tom at 123 clears it, and only while he is on-call.",
    "scenario_reroute": "Priya 139 online -> offline mid-Slack. Tom 123 clears floor 120. R3.",
    "scenario_floor": "set_on_call('stk-002', False) drops Tom to 108. Nothing online clears 120. R4 holds Priya on SMS and pages Elena.",
    "scenario_escalate": "Elena 140 comes online while Priya is in flight. 140 > 139 and severity CRITICAL. R9.",
    "scenario_failover": "logistics HIGH. Daniel 139 online sorts above Rashid 140 busy on reachability. Daniel prefers Slack; the adapter fails on connect; R6 fails over to email.",
    "guard": "No ONLINE person other than Priya (139) and Tom (123) reaches qualification >= 120 for infrastructure. The next highest is Daniel at 94."
  },

